  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '<b>Secure Networking V1.0</b>


    Secure Networking is a networking
    system for VRChat designed to prevent unauthorized players from modifying synced
    data. Instead of using normal Udon manual synchronization, it uses <b>network
    events with parameters</b>. This allows it to know exactly which player sent
    data and then verify if they are actually allowed to do so.


    Every network
    update is checked against the allowed senders before the data is applied. If
    the sender cannot be verified immediately, it can retry the update before eventually
    discarding it.


    It automatically keeps track of an <b>Authoritative Sender</b>,
    which is responsible for sending the current state to new players when they join.
    If the current sender leaves or is no longer allowed to send data, it  automatically
    tries to find another valid sender.


    Network updates also follow a <b>latest
    state wins</b> system. This how ever means that intermediate states are not guaranteed
    to be received.


    To use Secure Networking, a script inherits from <b>SecureNetworkBehaviour</b>
    and defines who is allowed to send data, what data should be sent, and how received
    data should be applied. A <b>SecureNetworkingInstance</b> then handles the actual
    networking, sender validation, authority management, and synchronization.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
